WEBVTT

NOTE
Narration of the Agent Kourier demo (docs/brand/film/narration.json, "demo").
Cue times read from the 16:9 render with ffmpeg silencedetect.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.800
You've put AI agents on Kubernetes.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.450
They can read logs, check rollouts,
and find the cause.

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.950
But they only work when someone
opens a prompt and asks.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.600
Alerts fire in your monitoring.

5
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.300
Questions come up in chat.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.300
Your agents hear neither.

7
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.450
Introducing Agent Kourier:

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.650
a Kubernetes-native broker between team chat
and A2A agents.

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:30.400
An alert, or a question, becomes an agent session,
in the thread where it landed.

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.600
Slack today.

11
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:39.450
When an alert lands in the channel, Agent Kourier picks it up,
opens the thread, and hands it to your agent.

12
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.850
It investigates right there, step by step,
and reports what it found.

13
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:50.400
Reply in the thread,
and the same session continues.

14
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.950
Same context, nothing re-explained.

15
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.700
Or skip the alert, and just ask.

16
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.650
When the agent needs a decision,
it asks, and waits for your answer.

17
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.950
Teams add one Binding, in YAML,
next to their agent.

18
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.250
The platform wiring is shared.

19
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.500
It works with kagent,
or any A2A agent that streams.

20
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.900
It's a two-way session: it answers as it works,
asks when it needs you, and keeps the context when you reply.

21
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.050
Slack today; more chat platforms are planned.

22
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.650
Agent Kourier.

23
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.450
Write the agent, not the chat integration.
